+### Repairing the guest network
+
+The preinstalled image sometimes boots with `eth0` unconfigured
+(`ifup` fails on a stale `/run/network/ifstate`), so DNS and HTTP
+fail with "Network is unreachable".  `guest-netfix.sh` attaches
+pfinet statically to the QEMU user-mode network (`10.0.2.15/24`,
+gateway `10.0.2.2`, DNS `10.0.2.3`) and verifies DNS and HTTP:
+
+```console
+$ python3 hurd_vm.py debian-hurd-amd64-20260314.img guest-netfix.sh
+```
+
+### Testing inference-translator fully offline
+
+The image ships `gcc` and `make` but no autoconf/automake/git.  To
+build and test [inference-translator](https://github.com/GNU-AI-SOFTWARE/inference-translator)
+without relying on the guest network: pre-generate `configure` on the
+host, pack the tree, inject it into the CI image with `inject-src.sh`,
+then run `guest-inference.sh` (it runs `make check`, mounts
+`/inference` with `settrans` and exercises the translator through
+plain POSIX commands):
+
+```console
+$ git clone https://github.com/GNU-AI-SOFTWARE/inference-translator ~/inference-translator
+$ cd ~/inference-translator && autoreconf -i && cd ~
+$ tar czf inference-src.tar.gz inference-translator
+$ ./inject-src.sh debian-hurd-amd64-20260314.img ~/inference-src.tar.gz
+$ python3 hurd_vm.py debian-hurd-amd64-20260314.img guest-inference.sh --ram 2G
+```
+
